NNAAMMEE
       swapon, swapoff - enable/disable devices and files for paging and
       swapping

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       sswwaappoonn [options] [_s_p_e_c_i_a_l_f_i_l_e...]

       sswwaappooffff [--vvaa] [_s_p_e_c_i_a_l_f_i_l_e...]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       sswwaappoonn is used to specify devices on which paging and swapping are to
       take place.

       The device or file used is given by the _s_p_e_c_i_a_l_f_i_l_e parameter. It may
       be of the form --LL _l_a_b_e_l or --UU _u_u_i_d to indicate a device by label or
       uuid.

       Calls to sswwaappoonn normally occur in the system boot scripts making all
       swap devices available, so that the paging and swapping activity is
       interleaved across several devices and files.

       sswwaappooffff disables swapping on the specified devices and files. When the
       --aa flag is given, swapping is disabled on all known swap devices and
       files (as found in _/_p_r_o_c_/_s_w_a_p_s or _/_e_t_c_/_f_s_t_a_b).

